/-
ZetaQ/PayoffSmooth.lean — **§11's feasibility certificates for the SMOOTH design profiles
`v = p²` of `ZetaQ/DesignProfile.lean`**, and the §11 link (stated).

An earlier form of §11's certificate proved `min B ≤ 2 − Pcert` with piecewise-polynomial
profiles (`Payoff.certQQ`, `certDyad`: degree 4 / 2, two cells) that the CONSTRUCTION never used —
the window it built was the flat taper, whose payoff is `B(v_flat) = 1.4086`. The construction now
realises the profile-weighted window `φ = p(u/ℒ)·ϱ₂(…)` with `p = designProfile F`, so the
certificate must be for `v = p²/∫p²` ON THE DESIGN SUPPORT `[−λ*/2, λ*/2]` — which is what
`certQQsmooth` / `certDyadSmooth` are: the SAME exact-ℚ engine (`two_cell_payoff'`, evaluating the
payoff per certificate rather than once for the file), the same two cells `[0, 1 − b]`,
`[1 − b, b]` with `b = λ*/2` EXACTLY (so `1 − b` is an interior node, `Cert.hmesh`), degree 12
(`p²`). The data were generated by the authoring project's
`profile_design.py` and exact-ℚ certificate engine, neither of which is shipped; nothing below
depends on them, since every constant here is a Lean literal and the feasibility statements are
proved from it in this file (Bernstein nonnegativity passes at the native degree 12; the mass
identity `2∫₀^b v = 1` is exact in ℚ).

Certified constants: `Pcert_qQ_smooth = 0.7212` (`B = 1.27874639`, slack `5.4·10⁻⁵` at the crude
`π⁴/18 ≤ 5.412`), `Pcert_dyad_smooth = 0.7098` (`B = 1.29015911`; the paper's `0.7099` is NOT
reached by a degree-6 `p` at the FIXED support `λ*_dyad/2` — recorded; the old `certDyad`'s
`0.7099` stands as a feasibility statement about a different profile).

The §11 link — `B(v_design) ≤ B(p²) + O(w/ℒ)` — is STATED (`ProfileRampLink`) with the
`Payoff.Gates`-style banner; its proof is deferred (see the docstring for exactly what it needs).

Imports `ZetaQ.DesignProfile`; imported by `Cor3Smooth`, `FrobRow8`, `RampLink`, `JoinCert`
and `HFrob`.
RULE 17: the bandwidths are the literals `λ* = 1.2507321515 > 1`, `λ*_dyad = 1.1931581210 > 1`.
-/
