    ∃ v : ℝ → ℝ, Admissible lamStarDyadic v ∧
      B (2 * Real.pi ^ 4 / 27) v ≤ 2 - ((Pcert_dyad_smooth : ℚ) : ℝ) := by
  obtain ⟨hadm, hB⟩ :=
    payoff_of_cert_num certDyadSmooth certDyadSmooth_NonnegOK certDyadSmooth_MassOK
      B0_certDyadSmooth B1_certDyadSmooth B0B1_certDyadSmooth.1 B0B1_certDyadSmooth.2
      (2 * Real.pi ^ 4 / 27) (2 * 3141593 ^ 4 / (27 * 10 ^ 24)) Pcert_dyad_smooth (by norm_num)
      C_dyad_le (by norm_num [B0_certDyadSmooth, B1_certDyadSmooth, Pcert_dyad_smooth])
  refine ⟨certDyadSmooth.toFun, ?_, hB⟩
  have hl : ((certDyadSmooth.lam : ℚ) : ℝ) = lamStarDyadic := by
    norm_num [Cert.lam, certDyadSmooth, lamStarDyadic]
  rwa [hl] at hadm

/-! ## 3. The §11 link — STATED (F58 item 7)

`κ_C = B(v)` for the profile the construction actually chooses: the
construction's profile is `v_design = φ²/∫φ²` in the scale-free variable, which is the design
polynomial's `p²` on the plateau and the ramp's `p²ϱ₂²` on the two strips of width `w/ℒ`. The link
is the comparison of `B` between the two, with an explicit `O(w/ℒ)` ramp cost. -/

/-- the construction's normalised profile in the scale-free variable `t = u/ℒ`:
`v_design(t) = φ(tℒ)² / ∫φ(sℒ)² ds = φ(tℒ)²·ℒ/(aL)`. -/
def vDesign (P : ParamsQ) (t : ℝ) : ℝ := (P.phiQ (t * P.LL)) ^ 2 * P.LL / (P.LB * P.aQ)

/-- the certified profile: `p²` on the design support, normalised. -/
def vProfile (P : ParamsQ) (t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  if |t| ≤ P.lam / 2 then
    (P.prof.eval t) ^ 2 / ∫ s in (-(P.lam / 2))..(P.lam / 2), (P.prof.eval s) ^ 2
  else 0

/-- the explicit ramp cost the link is expected to carry: the two ramp strips have total
measure `2w/ℒ`, both profiles are `≤ 2/λ` there (`a ≥ 3/4`, `p ≤ 1`), and `B` is quadratic with
kernel `≤ C·λ`, which gives `|B(v_design) − B(v_profile)| ≤ 64·(1 + C)·(w/ℒ)`. PROVED with room
(`RampLink.lean`: the achieved constant is `224/9·(1+C)` at `λ ≥ 1`). -/
def rampCost (C : ℝ) (P : ParamsQ) : ℝ := 64 * (1 + C) * (P.w / P.LL)

/-- **✅ THE §11 LINK — PROVED in `ZetaQ/RampLink.lean` (`Payoff.profileRampLink`).**
For every valid design point with `8w ≤ L` AND the bandwidth floor `1 ≤ λ`:
`B(v_design) ≤ B(v_profile) + rampCost`. ⚠ The floor is NECESSARY: the `1 ≤ λ`-free form first
stated here is FALSE (counterexample in `RampLink.lean`: `prof = 1`, `w = 1`, `8w = L`, `λ → 0`).
The design of record has `λ = λ* > 1`, so nothing downstream changes. The general λ-explicit
bound under `Valid` alone is `B_vDesign_le_explicit`: `B(v_design) ≤ B(v_profile) +
(128/(9λ²) + (32/3)(1+C))·(w/ℒ)`.

Original statement note (kept): for every valid design point with
`8w ≤ L`: `B(v_design) ≤ B(v_profile) + rampCost`. Together with `payoff_feasible_*_smooth`
(`B(v_profile) ≤ 2 − Pcert` at the design profile) this is what turns `frobenius_row`'s
`κ_C + rowR2` into a bound the construction actually attains (`κ_C := B(v_design)` up to
`O(w/ℒ)`, which is budget row `L₆`'s shape).

What a proof needs (recorded): (i) `vDesign P` and `vProfile P` are both admissible at `λ`
(`vDesign`: nonneg, integrable, mass 1 by `Valid.aQ_eq_av` and the change of variables `u = tℒ`,
support `|t| ≤ λ/2` from `Valid.phiQ_eq_zero`; `vProfile`: the same with `ProfileQ`);
(ii) they agree on `|t| ≤ λ/2 − w/ℒ` up to the normalisation ratio `∫p²/(aλ) = 1 + O(w/ℒ)`
(`ParamsQ.core_integral_le` and its converse from `φ ≤ p`, `DesignProfile.lean` §3);
(iii) `B` is `2·sup‖·‖∞·(1 + Cλ)·λ`-Lipschitz in `L¹` on profiles bounded by `2/λ`
(`Payoff.B` is `ψ(0) + ∫Wψ` with `ψ = v⋆v`, `W ≤ max(1, C)·λ` on `supp ψ ⊆ [−λ, λ]`);
(iv) the `L¹` distance is `≤ 2·(w/ℒ)·(2/λ) + |1 − ratio|`. None of (i)–(iv) is new
analysis; the constant `64` in `rampCost` is what this bookkeeping should deliver and must be
re-derived when the proof is written. -/
def ProfileRampLink : Prop :=
  ∀ (C : ℝ) (P : ParamsQ), 0 ≤ C → P.Valid → 8 * P.w ≤ P.LB → 1 ≤ P.lam →
    B C (vDesign P) ≤ B C (vProfile P) + rampCost C P

end Payoff
end ZetaQ

end
